  "notes": "Drawn from 2025-26 photos of A321neos VN-A552 (left), VN-A653 (right) and VN-A543 (left, below). The slogan differs by side (Vietnamese on the left, English on the right). Many VietJet aircraft carry advertising over the white forward fuselage (e.g. VN-A653 in 2024); this is the plain scheme. Titles on the fin are turned along it, which the title fields can't express. The logo is the wordmark itself, so no tail-symbol shape; the engine star's shape is given. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on VN-A552 (left, from behind: placed between the overwing exits and the aft door) and VN-A653 (right, square on): the fuselage title isn't placed the same on the two sides. On the left it runs x 0.49 to 0.715 (it starts about 2 m behind the color bands); on the right x 0.565 to 0.76, its 'v' about 4 m ahead of the aft door. Now a pair of titles, one per side. The slogans: 'Bay là Thích ngay!' x 0.68 to 0.79, 'Enjoy Flying!' 0.745 to 0.805; the fin title runs from near the root up to the tip, about 1.05 of the root chord; the belly title's length (0.2) is a rough read from below (low). The aft yellow band and the white tail cone are curves: smooth; the forward color bands are straight from the side.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Essentially unchanged since the airline's launch (2011; the scheme was shown 2007); Thai VietJet (TVJ) and VietJet Thailand wear it with Thai details."
}
